# TASK-260715-3cv3r4 test outcome

## Result

Ready for review. The task-scoped SwiftPM suites are deterministic, fake-only, and passing. No real Keychain or network runtime was used.

## Implemented coverage

- Profile snapshot table/loop matrices cover canonical DNS/IPv4/IPv6/IDNA forms, malformed hosts, scalar fields, schema/protocol transitions, canonical JSON, trust ordering/state, prohibited fields, envelope validation, immutable generations, and concurrent atomic capture.
- Invalid profile payloads assert zero fake Keychain and zero fake network calls before the validation boundary returns an error.
- Keychain tests use inert fixture handles only. They assert the exact single system-domain search-list query, fixed service/reference, one-item limit, no access-group/fallback/enumeration keys, inaccessible/malformed/generation/passphrase cases, cancellation clearing, signer retirement, and malformed-reference zero calls.
- Host policy tests cover first use, approved match, change, sequential rotation, exact revocation, canonical host/port mismatch, unsupported algorithms, malformed evidence, and redacted printable values.
- Candidate-neutral pre-auth fixtures assert `hostPolicy -> credentialLookup -> authentication`; every rejecting host decision stops after `hostPolicy` with zero authentication/channel calls.
- Bootstrap/error tests cover the stable golden taxonomy, all credential resolver projections, POSIX/DNS/TLS normalization, cancellation, runtime diagnostic snapshot storage/clearing, and prohibited-data redaction.
- Bounded tests execute 16 credential/secret iterations and 16 pre-auth connection iterations, restoring active secret containers and fake task/channel/socket/descriptor/buffer counts to zero each time.

